      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$ is the set of all positive real numbers and zero.\n\n- $0$: Zero is included by the subscript $0$. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $\\sqrt{25}=5$: It is positive, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $-\\pi$: It is negative, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $-3\\sqrt{6}$: It is negative, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $0$; $\\sqrt{25}$.",
