      ":question/id": "2fad31cf-b8e4-555d-bf55-9e3f81258d5d",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the numbers below belong to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$ is the set of all negative integers and zero.\n\n- $8.2=\\frac{41}{5}$: It is positive, and it is a rational number but not an integer, since it can be written as $\\frac{41}{5}$. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $\\sqrt{16}=4$: It is positive, and it is an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $\\frac{27}{3}=9$: It is positive, and it is an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $\\sqrt{31}$: It is positive, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: None of those listed.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
