      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$ is the set of all negative rational numbers.\n\n- $-2\\sqrt{2}$: It is negative, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $-\\frac{34}{2}=-17$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $-\\sqrt{49}=-7$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $-\\frac{2}{8}=-\\frac{1}{4}$: It is negative, and it is a rational number but not an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $-\\frac{34}{2}$; $-\\sqrt{49}$; $-\\frac{2}{8}$.",
